[agent:result]   You can use a serving endpoint to serve models from the Databricks Model
[agent:result]   Registry or from Unity Catalog. Endpoints expose the underlying models as
[agent:result]   scalable REST API endpoints using serverless compute. This means the endpoints
[agent:result]   and associated compute resources are fully managed by Databricks and will not
[agent:result]   appear in your cloud account. A serving endpoint can consist of one or more
[agent:result]   MLflow models from the Databricks Model Registry, called served entities. A
[agent:result]   serving endpoint can have at most ten served entities. You can configure
[agent:result]   traffic settings to define how requests should be routed to your served
[agent:result]   entities behind an endpoint. Additionally, you can configure the scale of
[agent:result]   resources that should be applied to each served entity.
